## The scenario conversations are opened on

A new conversation is opened on the scenario `ScenarioResolverInterface` gives. By default, `ConfiguredScenarioResolver`: the one the configuration names.

```yaml
syrtis_symfony_client:
    scenario: '%env(SYRTIS_CHAT_SCENARIO)%'
```

An application keeping that choice elsewhere — the version noted at each deployment — aliases the interface to its own service:

```yaml
# config/services.yaml
SyrtisSymfonyClient\Interface\ScenarioResolverInterface: '@App\Service\Scenario\AgentChatScenarioResolver'
```

A conversation keeps the scenario it was opened on: a new one is opened on the scenario resolved then.

## When Syrtis refuses a turn

A turn Syrtis does not take — no such scenario, a key it does not know — is logged, and said in the conversation as an `error` turn: the page the account wrote from does not fail.
